course: dictionary
lesson: 10120
title: Thorough: done with care
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Thorough means done completely, carefully and with attention to every detail. A thorough check looks at every part, so nothing gets missed. The words around it give you clues about what is being checked and how hard.
explain: «A thorough search looks everywhere.» Search tells you someone was looking for something, and thorough tells you they looked in every place, slowly and carefully. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a complete, careful search" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: A person can be thorough too. A thorough person is careful to do everything well, and does not skip the small jobs. Thorough and thoroughly are related: «wash your hands thoroughly» means wash them completely, with care.
fact: Thorough means done completely, carefully and with attention to every detail.
fact: «A thorough check» means a check that misses nothing.
fact: In school, a thorough answer covers every part of the question.
fact: «Thoroughly» is the adverb, as in «wash your hands thoroughly».
fact: In informal British English, thorough can mean complete or total, as in «a thorough nuisance».
exercise: «Real notes carry security features, so fakes are hard to make and easy to spot.» A thorough check of a note would look at what? | Nothing, because notes are always real | *Every security feature, such as the see-through window | A quick glance and then stop | Only the colour of the front
exercise: In science, a thorough investigation does what? | *Repeats tests and checks the results | Uses one test and then stops | Avoids looking at the results | Finishes in one minute
exercise: Ella checks her bike before riding, every brake, tyre and light. Which word fits her check? | Glum | *Thorough | Curt | Barely
test: «She gave a thorough answer that covered every part of the question.» What does thorough mean here? | Quick and short | Rude and unfriendly | Very loud | *Done completely, covering every part
test: Which word is the adverb? «Wash your hands ___.» | thoroughness | thorough | *thoroughly | thorougher
exam: «A thorough search looks everywhere.» What does a thorough search do? | *Looks in every place, carefully | Looks only for fun | Stops after one minute | Looks in one place only
